(926: (meta: (t: semantic) (n: 1) (term: string%20value) (def: %23%20Private%20B95%20borrowed-outcome%20probe%0A%0AThese%20are%20source-only%20proposals%20for%20the%20separately%20authenticated%20scratch%20crate%0Aoverlay.%20Their%20author%20has%20executed%20no%20oracle%2C%20test%2C%20formatter%2C%20native%20compiler%2C%0ACargo%20command%2C%20generator%20or%20download.%20No%20repository%20file%20is%20changed%20by%20this%0Apacket.%20Native%20compilation%20and%20observations%20remain%20unverified%20until%20future%20CI.%0A%0A%60oracle.mjs%60%20uses%20the%20original%20checkout%27s%20actual%20public%20JavaScript%20grammar%20and%0Astructured-data%20APIs.%20Its%20only%20output%20is%20an%20explicitly%20supplied%20file%20outside%0Athat%20checkout.%20The%20producer%20retains%20listings%2C%20input%20strings%20or%20exact%20byte%20arrays%2C%0Aresolver%20bindings%20and%20options%2C%20then%20freshly%20parses%20every%20real%20outcome.%20It%20encodes%0Aexpectations%20as%20ordinary%20Links%20data%20through%20the%20existing%20writer.%20This%20is%20an%0Aauthored%20oracle%20fixture%2C%20not%20a%20retained%20production%20observation%20receipt.%0A%0A%60%60%60sh%0Anode%20%2Fprivate%2Ftmp%2Fmeta-language-bulk95-outcome-native-probe%2Foracle.mjs%20%5C%0A%20%20--repository%20ORIGINAL_CHECKOUT%20--output%20PRIVATE_SCRATCH%2Foracle.lino%0A%60%60%60%0A%0AThe%20runner%20must%20pin%20these%20source%20files%20and%20the%20unchanged%20original%20checkout%20before%0Arunning%20that%20command%20once.%20It%20may%20copy%20%60bulk95_outcome_probe.rs%60%20only%20into%20the%0Ascratch%20overlay%20at%20%60rust%2Ftests%2Fbulk95_outcome_probe.rs%60.%20No%20manifest%20or%20lockfile%0Achange%2C%20new%20dependency%2C%20test-root%20registration%20or%20production%20API%20change%20is%20needed.%0AThe%20candidate%20must%20remain%20inside%20the%20actual%20library%20because%20its%20encoder%20uses%0Acrate-private%20graph%20operations.%20The%20probe%20imports%20its%20temporary%20API%20from%0A%60meta_language%3A%3Astructured_data_links%60%2C%20without%20a%20new%20crate-root%20alias.%0A%0AThe%20separately%20owned%20runner%20supplies%3A%0A%0A-%20%60META_LANGUAGE_B95_OUTCOME_FIXTURE%60%3A%20the%20absolute%20fresh%20oracle%20%60.lino%60%20path.%0A-%20%60META_LANGUAGE_B95_OUTCOME_REPORT%60%3A%20the%20retained%20private%20assertion%20report%20path.%0A-%20Its%20explicit%20CI%2FLinux%20opt-in%20and%20independent%20bounded%20Cargo%2Fartifact%20deadlines.%0A%0AThe%20probe%20uses%20only%20existing%20normal%2Fdev%20dependencies.%20It%20never%20starts%20Node%2C%0Aanother%20compiler%20or%20a%20subprocess.%20The%20runner%27s%20default%20plan%2Fcheck%20must%20do%20no%0Aoracle%20or%20Cargo%20work%3B%20future%20native%20work%20requires%20its%20explicit%20CI%20opt-in.%20The%0Aprivate%20report%20is%20written%20through%20the%20old%20generic%20codec%20only%20after%20every%20native%0Aassertion%20has%20held.%20It%20does%20not%20call%20requirement-ledger%20observation%20functions.%0A%0A%23%23%20Finite%20assertions%20proposed%0A%0AEleven%20freshly%20parsed%20cases%20cover%20accepted%20UTF-8%2C%20syntax%20rejection%2C%20automatic%0Arecovery%20accepted%2Frefused%2C%20actual%20semantic-action%20attribute%20order%2C%20any-grammar%0Aalternatives%20and%20ambiguity%20refusal%2C%20recursive%20nested%20selection%2C%20included-range%0Asource%20planes%20with%20existing%20mapped-tree%20validation%2C%20unknown%20grammar%20rejection%2C%0Aand%20a%20malformed%20UTF-8%20byte%20accepted%20by%20%60any%60%20and%20retained%20as%20a%20Hex%20leaf.%0A%0AThree%20independent%2C%20explicitly%20constructed%20values%20cover%20required%20nulls%3B%20all%20five%0ASyntaxTree%20variants%3B%20both%20LeafText%20variants%3B%20both%20OperationValue%20variants%3B%0Aall%20nine%20typed%20declarations%3B%20absent%20versus%20present%20empty%2Fnull%20option%20values%3B%0Afalse%20flag%20omission%3B%20ordered%20opaque%20values%2C%20lexical%20metadata%2C%20selection%20and%0Aalternative%20metadata%3B%20signed%20zero%3B%20exact%20large%20integers%3B%20and%20repeated%20scalar%0Aoccurrences.%20These%20values%20are%20authored%20independently%20of%20the%20candidate.%20Their%0Asynthetic%20source%2Fselection%20metadata%20is%20not%20claimed%20to%20pass%20a%20grammar%2C%20action%0Alanguage%2C%20ownership%2C%20provenance%20or%20mapped-tree%20validator.%0A%0AFor%20every%20row%20the%20native%20probe%20compares%20the%20complete%20ordered%20value%20and%20actual%0Abinary64%20bits%20with%20the%20fixture%2C%20including%20-0.%20It%20then%20checks%20exact%20text%20and%20binary%0Areplay%20of%20each%20actual%20native%20graph%2C%20retaining%20its%20own%20IDs%2Freferences%2Fmetadata%20and%0Abinary%20bytes.%20The%20constructed%20signed-zero%20case%20also%20asserts%20the%20actual%20scalar%0Adefinition%20is%20%60-0%60.%20Replay%20uses%20separate%20sufficient%20historical%20decoder%2Fbinary%0Alimits%3B%20serialized%20input%20size%20is%20never%20compared%20to%20the%20candidate%27s%20exact%0Ascalar-byte%20budget.%20It%20never%20compares%20native%20graph%20IDs%2C%20physical%20node%20counts%20or%20alias%0Aidentity%20with%20JavaScript%27s%20graph.%20JavaScript%27s%20generic%20encoder%20can%20preserve%0Acontainer%20sharing%3B%20native%20owned%20inputs%20do%20not%20describe%20equivalent%20shared%20owners.%0A%0ALimits%20are%20obtained%20by%20independently%20traversing%20the%20existing%20JavaScript%20codec%27s%0Aactual%20graph%2C%20expanding%20every%20reference%20and%20counting%20its%20actual%20scalar-definition%0AUTF-8%20bytes.%20Schema%20root%20is%20depth%20zero%20and%20counted%20last%3B%20object%20pair%2Fkey%2Fvalue%20and%0Aarray%20depths%20come%20from%20graph%20references%2C%20without%20a%20replacement%20serializer.%20Each%0Arow%20tests%20all%20three%20exact%20limits%20and%20one-below%20refusal%20separately.%20Repeated%20scalar%0Areferences%20demonstrate%20expanded%20counts%20differ%20from%20physical%20graph%20allocation.%0AAdditional%20native%20boundaries%20cover%20zero%20limits%2C%20depth%20setting%20257%2C%20a%20300-node%0Aconstructed%20nesting%20chain%2C%20a%201024-byte%20scalar%20against%20a%2064-byte%20budget%2C%20integer%0Arounding%20refusal%20in%20both%20opaque%20Number%20and%20OperationValue%20positions%2C%20and%20an%0Aarbitrary%20native%20IndexMap%20key%20order%20which%20JavaScript%20ordinary%20objects%20would%20sort%0Adifferently.%20That%20last%20native-owned%20assertion%20has%20an%20independent%20ordered%20expected%0Avalue%20and%20is%20explicitly%20not%20JavaScript%20parser%20parity.%0A%0A%23%23%20Limits%20of%20the%20proposed%20evidence%0A%0ANo%20public%2Fdefault%20CST%20API%2C%20unchanged-source%20alias%2C%20physical%20graph%20identity%2C%0Aassociation%20ownership%2C%20source-plane%20provenance%20authentication%2C%20broad%20language%0Asupport%2C%20arbitrary-depth%20stack%20safety%2C%20all%20allocator-failure%20recovery%2C%20or%20other%0Aplatform%20parity%20is%20established.%20The%20first%20proposed%20runner%20is%20Linux%20CI%20only.%0AThe%20candidate%20deliberately%20refuses%20depth%20settings%20above%20256%3B%20the%20old%20generic%0Acodec%27s%20limits%20and%20behavior%20are%20not%20changed.%20Byte%20budget%20means%20expanded%20scalar%0Adefinitions%2C%20not%20serialized%20text%2Fbinary%20size.%0A%0APublic%20native%20strings%20are%20UTF-8%20and%20serde_json%3A%3ANumber%20cannot%20contain%20NaN%20or%0AInfinity.%20This%20probe%20does%20not%20fabricate%20those%20as%20native%20values%20or%20claim%20isolated%0AUTF-16%20surrogate%20support%20in%20the%20ParseOutcome%20domain.%20Exact%20number%20formatting%20is%0Athe%20original%20production%20codec%27s%20helper%2C%20not%20an%20independent%20new%20algorithm.%20The%0A2%5E53%20and%20i64%3A%3AMIN%20constructed%20operation%20values%20test%20the%20enum%27s%20transport%20domain%2C%0Anot%20the%20documented%20safe-integer%20operation-language%20admission%20policy.%0A%0AUntil%20the%20CI%20artifact%20runs%2C%20both%20actual%20native%20compilation%2FAPI%20compatibility%20and%0Aall%20native%20outcome%2Fvalue%2Fbudget%20assertions%20above%20remain%20proposals%2C%20not%20results.%0A) (lang: meta-language%20structured%20data)))
